      "content": "<h3>Use ArrayList or something else?</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;\">\n<tr><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Use ArrayList when</th><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Use something else when</th></tr>\n<tr><td>You read by index a lot</td><td>You insert or remove at the front all the time: use <code>ArrayDeque</code> or <code>LinkedList</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>You mostly add at the end and then loop</td><td>You need \"is this present?\" checks fast: use <code>HashSet</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>The order of insertion matters</td><td>You need the data always sorted: use <code>TreeSet</code> or <code>TreeMap</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Duplicates are fine</td><td>You must forbid duplicates: use <code>Set</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>One thread uses the list</td><td>Many threads change it: use <code>CopyOnWriteArrayList</code> or a concurrent queue</td></tr>\n</table>"
