      "content": "<h3>1. add(E e)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>boolean add(E e)</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> <code>true</code> (always, for ArrayList)</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1) amortised</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Puts the element at the <strong>end</strong> of the list. The list grows by one. You do not have to check the size first.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Normally just writes into the next free slot of the internal array. When the array is full it allocates a bigger one (about 1.5 times) and copies, which is why the cost is called <em>amortised</em> O(1): rare expensive growths are spread over many cheap adds. Every structural change also increases <code>modCount</code>, which makes running iterators fail fast.</p>",
