      "content": "<h3>4. addAll(int index, Collection c)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>boolean addAll(int index, Collection<? extends E> c)</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> <code>true</code> if the list changed</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(n + m)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Inserts a whole collection <strong>in the middle</strong>: the new elements go in at <code>index</code> (in their own order) and the old elements after it shift to the right.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> One shift of the tail plus one copy of the new block. Prefer it over a loop of <code>add(i, e)</code> calls, which would shift the tail once per element.</p>",
